A||||3||batboy||RCC bump steer kit update||||1||
Z||000000||batboy||02-18-2000||06:29 PM||||In another one of my recent topics, Phil mentioned the RCC bump steer kit as being a low cost alternative to the Ryane kit. While the SCCA racers are probably lined up and drooling at the Ryane kit complete with tubular replacement control arms, they are kind of pricey.<P>What about us poor budget minded hi-po street guys? I'd rather look towards the RCC kit which is only $120 plus about $10 shipping in my case (Texas to Kansas). This sounds like a good compromise for serious street driving.<P>I emailed RCC and got back a quick reply from Darrel who confirmed that they do still have the bump steer kits available for the older Fieros (non-88). I'm going to send off for a kit right away. I'll report more when I get it installed.<p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 02-18-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||pherder||02-18-2000||07:31 PM||||Batboy,<P>See my comments on the other thread!!!<P>Paul||||reg||3
Z||000002||batboy||02-22-2000||08:52 PM||||I wrote back and asked for more info on the RCC rear coil-overs, recommended spring rates, and whether or not I could get a price break if I ordered both the coil-over kit and the bump steer kit.<P><B>REPLY FROM RCC:</B> We use the premium gas charged Gabriel OEM replacement strut.  As to spring rate, while you indicated a GM 350 engine, there was no hint as to the hp or torque of the engine. While a 300# spring rate will be fully adequate to support the weight and provide a reasonable firm ride. If you have 300+ hp or 350+ tq this could suggest a slightly higher spring rate. The higher the hp/torque, the more spring required to provide adequate low to moderate speed stability under heavy acceleration.<P>As to price, since we introduced the coilover strut we have already absorbed 2 price increases on the struts, and price increases on all of the other parts and pieces.  Add increases in salaries, rent, etc. and we are about to the point that we will have to increase our prices.  No room to play fast and loose with discounts.  --Darrel <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||fieroshop||02-22-2000||09:17 PM||||I just installed a set of RCC bump steer kit and they are very easy to install. By the looks of things it will work fairly well, not as good as Ryan's bump steer kit, I will be purchasing a unit for my shop and try it on my Blue 87 GT that I am restoring and which is for sale. ||||reg||1
